the templates are:
    *a person* knows that *a number* will win the lottery; unknown.
    *a person* becomes rich.
    *a person* bets *a number* timely.
    *a payment* is in respect of *a claim*.
    *a payment* is processed.
    *a payment* is approved.
    *a payment* is finalized.

the knowledge base unknowns includes:

it is unknown whether a payment is in respect of claim 01.

a person becomes rich if
    the person knows that a number will win the lottery and
    the person bets the number timely.

a payment is processed if
    the payment is in respect of a claim.

a payment is finalized if
    the payment is approved.

scenario one is:
    alice bets 42 timely.
    bob bets 7 timely.
    bob knows that 7 will win the lottery.
    one expects answers [
        "alice becomes rich",
        "bob becomes rich"
    ] and unknowns [
        "alice knows that 42 will win the lottery"
    ].

scenario two is:
    two expects answers [
        "payment 100 is processed"
    ] and unknowns [
        "payment 100 is in respect of claim 1"
    ].

scenario three is:
    payment 100 is in respect of claim 01.
    two expects answers [
        "payment 100 is processed"
    ] and unknowns [].

scenario four is:
    it is unknown whether a payment is approved.
    three expects answers [
        "payment 200 is finalized"
    ] and unknowns [
        "payment 200 is approved"
    ].

scenario five is:
    payment 200 is approved.
    three expects answers [
        "payment 200 is finalized"
    ] and unknowns [].

query one is:
    which person becomes rich.

query two is:
    payment 100 is processed.

query three is:
    payment 200 is finalized.
